Sat Oct 17 17:42:53 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to version 1.522:
  * Thousands of redrawn and added Hanzi: BIG5 completed,
    Extension A reworked per GB/Z 40637-2021, Extension A redraws
    shared with fellow Klee-derived projects, plus new
    superscript/subscript letters.
  * Bold weight renamed to Medium; Hanzi widths unified to 1 EM;
    macOS/iOS Medium rendering and mono isFixedPitch fixed.
  * New OpenType features: halt/vhal and experimental chws/vchw
    punctuation squeezing, dash ligation, ccmp combining marks
    for pinyin, UVS centered-punctuation variants; mono drops
    dlig which harmed editor rendering.
  * Vertical metrics adjusted to fix oversized vertical spacing;
    minus sign unified with plus width; U+2E3A/2E3B set to 1 EM.
  * Korean: all 11,172 syllables completed, compatibility jamo
    added, KPS 9566 and GB/T 12052 syllables covered.
  * New symbols: ancient Chinese punctuation, counting-rod
    numerals, IBM Plex Math-derived shapes; Light-weight symbols
    partly restored to Klee One originals.
  * Many more glyph adjustments; see upstream release notes.

